================================================================
1. CORRECT PREVIOUS CLAIMS
================================================================

Upgrade-20 report explicitly stated:

Task lifecycle:
    no real task persistence

Worktree:
    no real git worktree

Checkpoint recovery:
    in-memory only

Do not carry these forward as production durability.

Use:

CONTRACT_PROVEN
SYSTEM_PROVEN
DURABILITY_NOT_PROVEN

until executed evidence exists.

================================================================
2. DURABLE ENGINEERING STORE
================================================================

Create/consolidate:

EngineeringStore

Responsibilities:

tasks
attempts
plans
checkpoints
worktrees
validation results
review results
approvals
commits
remote operations
CI state

Do not create one database per subsystem unnecessarily.

================================================================
3. STORAGE INTERFACE
================================================================

Provide clean storage abstraction.

Required implementations:

SQLiteEngineeringStore
PostgresEngineeringStore

SQLite:

CORE_FREE
single-host durable operation

PostgreSQL:

SELF_HOSTED
multi-process coordination

================================================================
4. NO IN-MEMORY PRODUCTION DEFAULT
================================================================

InMemoryEngineeringStore may remain for tests.

It must never become default for:

local persistent mode
self-hosted mode
production mode

================================================================
5. TASK PERSISTENCE
================================================================

Persist complete EngineeringTask identity.

Restart process.

Reload same task.

Prove:

task_id unchanged
state unchanged
history intact

================================================================
6. ATTEMPT PERSISTENCE
================================================================

ExecutionAttempt must survive restart.

Retry creates:

new attempt

Resume restores:

existing attempt

Do not confuse retry and resume.

================================================================
7. STATE TRANSITIONS
================================================================

Persist transitions transactionally.

Invalid transition must fail.

Example:

SUCCEEDED
→ RUNNING

must not occur accidentally.

================================================================
8. STATE VERSION
================================================================

Add optimistic concurrency/version field where appropriate.

Prevent two workers from overwriting task state.

================================================================
9. CHECKPOINT PERSISTENCE
================================================================

Persist checkpoints durably.

Checkpoint fields should include:

task
attempt
phase
sequence
timestamp
state snapshot/reference
worktree
base commit
current commit
validation state

================================================================
10. CHECKPOINT ORDER
================================================================

Use monotonic checkpoint sequence.

Concurrent writers cannot reorder state silently.

================================================================
11. RESUME FROM PROCESS RESTART
================================================================

Required system test:

start task
reach checkpoint
terminate ZCoder process

start new ZCoder process

resume same task

No in-process Python object may be required.

================================================================
12. HARD CRASH TEST
================================================================

Do not test only graceful shutdown.

Kill worker process abruptly.

Restart.

Recover.

================================================================
13. SQLITE DURABILITY TEST
================================================================

Use actual SQLite file.

Process A:

create task/checkpoint

exit

Process B:

load/resume

Verify exact state.

================================================================
14. SQLITE TRANSACTION SAFETY
================================================================

Use appropriate transaction semantics.

Do not rely on application mutex alone.

================================================================
15. SQLITE WAL
================================================================

Evaluate SQLite WAL mode for local durability/concurrency.

Use it only if appropriate for current access pattern.

Document decision.

================================================================
16. POSTGRESQL ENGINEERING STORE
================================================================

Use existing PostgreSQL infrastructure.

Do not build second PostgreSQL stack.

Tenant-owned rows must remain organization/project scoped.

================================================================
17. POSTGRESQL RLS
================================================================

Engineering tasks/attempts/checkpoints owned by tenants require existing
RLS discipline.

Add policies where missing.

================================================================
18. MULTI-PROCESS WORKERS
================================================================

Run at least two independent OS processes against same PostgreSQL store.

Both attempt to claim engineering jobs.

Each task executes once.

================================================================
19. CLAIM LEASE
================================================================

Reuse existing lease/fencing mechanism.

Do not introduce a competing lease implementation.

================================================================
20. STALE WORKER
================================================================

Worker A owns task.

Lease expires / ownership moves to B.

A must not:

commit
push
create PR

after losing ownership.

================================================================
21. EXTERNAL MUTATION FENCE
================================================================

Immediately before:

commit if globally coordinated
push
PR create
PR update
merge

verify:

current authoritative ownership
attempt
generation/fence

